    "body": "### [starship-RPMs+debs.zip](https://github.com/starship/starship/files/4875662/starship-RPMs%2Bdebs.zip)\r\nhopefully the rpmspec/debspecs will be of further use. \r\n\r\n**Cargo EBUILD , however is borking a bit for this else I'd not care to even botheer to spinkles these ziped builds. \r\nas gentoo for platforms will just build... riscv-64 no problemo... powerpc , amd64 yup& yup....** \r\n\r\n****https://github.com/iqlusioninc/cargo-rpm**\r\nhttps://github.com/mmstick/cargo-deb**\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/gentoo/gentoo-rust/tree/master/dev-util/cargo-deb\r\n\r\ncargo install cargo-deb , cargo-rpm  (cargo-ebuild) however not bulding a valid ebuild\r\nfor Gentoo installs system-wide at emerge..  however cargo-install \r\n/home/user/ same with windows 10... \r\n\r\nfor arm64 sometimes cargo-rpm/deb builds/sometimes no... \r\n but from git clone on rpi4/deb aarch64 might have more luck. \r\n\r\nhowever gentoo rust overlay , emerge dose the git clone/upgrade/install etc less fuss for me. \r\n\r\n\r\nemerge layman or eselect-repository \r\nA: older layman , layman -L && layman -a rust\r\nB: newer mostly reliable less deps , eslect-repository \r\neslect repository add /enable rust \r\nemerge --sync rust to sync rust (gentoo-rust overlay )\r\n\r\nemerge dev-util/cargo-deb , cargo-rpm \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nwith these specs / debspecs can spin more rpms/ or debs etc in the aarch64 \r\n\r\n\r\n### https://github.com/sakaki-/gentoo-on-rpi-64bit\r\n\r\none 4-GIG RPI4 8 gigs would be gloruos. however most vendors are waitlisted. \r\n\r\n\r\nelse ubuntu or Debian rpi4 image/s ",
